\title{Barycentric cancellation below the top degree}
\taxon{Lemma}
\meta{status}{proof-account}
\meta{dependencies}{[Barycentric weights](cn-0030)}
\meta{provenance}{[OpenAI, 23 September 2026](cn-0042), equation (4.5); reconstructed as a reading account on 9 October 2026. [Lean source: NodeMoments](/source-material/openai-math/lean/OAI/Combinatorics/Crossing/NodeMoments.lean).}

\p{\strong{Statement.} For the [barycentric weights](cn-0030) on #{n} distinct nodes, every scalar polynomial #{A} of degree at most #{n-2} satisfies}

##{\sum_{p=1}^n w_p A(x_p)=0.}

\p{\strong{Proof.} Lagrange interpolation gives}

##{A(t)=\sum_p A(x_p)w_p\frac{F(t)}{t-x_p}.}

\p{Both sides have degree at most #{n-1} and agree at all #{n} nodes, so the identity follows from the root bound for polynomials. Each quotient #{F(t)/(t-x_p)} is monic of degree #{n-1}, whereas the coefficient of that degree in #{A} is zero. Comparing those coefficients proves the assertion.}
